Reinforcement Learning:

Reinforcement Learning is a trial-and-error learning process where a machine (agent) learns by interacting with an environment and getting rewards or penalties for its actions.

Why RL Works Better Here
•	RL learns from experience, not just fixed past data.
•	It adapts to new fraud tricks automatically.
•	The reward system teaches it to find the balance between catching fraud and not annoying customers.
•	Model adapts to new fraud patterns automatically

•	Now, we train an RL Agent (say using Deep Q-Learning):
•	It interacts with transactions one by one.
•	Each time it decides to Block/Approve, it gets a Reward.
Over time, it learns the best decision pattern.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Supervised Learning → Learn from labeled data
Unsupervised Learning → Find patterns
Reinforcement Learning → Learn from experience (reward/punishment)
